WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:10.054
Under Section 504 of the Criminal Code of Canada, any citizen — any Canadian — has the legal right to lay criminal charges through private prosecution.

00:00:10.054 --> 00:00:17.459
This page documents over one thousand sourced criminal charge incidents, mapped to specific government officials.

00:00:17.459 --> 00:00:20.720
Two hundred and seventy officials identified.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.559
Three hundred and seven charges mapped.

00:00:23.559 --> 00:00:33.777
Each entry includes the relevant Criminal Code section, the evidence basis from public records, and the prosecution pathway available to any Canadian citizen.

00:00:33.777 --> 00:00:35.597
This is your legal right.

00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:38.274
It has existed since Confederation.

00:00:38.274 --> 00:00:47.024
And it is the mechanism by which Canadians can hold their government accountable — without waiting for an RCMP that refuses to investigate.
